      "math_academy_id": "e-14829",
      "problem": "Solve $3p^2 = 5p.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we move all of the terms to the left-hand side and then factor:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t3p^2 &= 5p \\[3pt]\n\t3p^2 - 5p &= 0 \\[3pt]\n\tp(3p - 5) &= 0\n}\n$$\n\nSo, by the zero product rule, we have\n\n$$\np=0 \\qquad\\text{or}\\qquad 3p-5=0,\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives \n\n$$\np=0 \\qquad\\text{or}\\qquad p=\\dfrac{5}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $p=0,\\dfrac{5}{3}.$",
